Wait for the first picture of a camera reached through the Camera portal, or its failure

A camera reached through the Camera portal and PipeWire (patch 0009) starts as soon as
its stream is asked to connect, before PipeWire links the camera to it, so a camera that
cannot give pictures (another application holds it) still looked started, and the
application showed a black picture. RTCVideoCapturer::WaitForStart waits after
StartCapture, up to the time given, for the camera's first picture or for PipeWire's
stream to say it failed (VideoCaptureModule::CaptureFailed, patches/webrtc/0017), looking
every 50 ms on the cameras' thread. It tells kStartRunning for a picture, or at the end of
the time for a stream that runs with its first picture late (a camera slow to start);
kStartFailed with what the stream was told; kStartNoPicture, with the stream's state, for
a stream that did not even run in that time. Cameras opened directly (V4L2, and the other
systems' cameras) tell a failure as StartCapture returns and answer kStartRunning at
once; so does a capturer made outside the library that does not override it.

diff --git a/include/rtc_video_device.h b/include/rtc_video_device.h
index 4ccda60..cf5f6c3 100644
--- a/include/rtc_video_device.h
+++ b/include/rtc_video_device.h
@@ -14,6 +14,29 @@ class RTCVideoCapturer : public RefCountInterface {
   virtual bool CaptureStarted() = 0;
 
   virtual void StopCapture() = 0;
+
+  // How a camera's start went, as WaitForStart tells it.
+  enum StartOutcome {
+    // A picture came, or the camera's stream runs and its first picture is
+    // late ([why] says so), or the camera tells a failure as StartCapture
+    // returns, so there is nothing to wait for.
+    kStartRunning = 0,
+    // The system said the camera cannot give pictures; [why] says what it said.
+    kStartFailed = 1,
+    // Within the time no picture came and the stream did not even run; [why]
+    // says what it was doing.
+    kStartNoPicture = 2,
+  };
+
+  // Waits, after StartCapture, up to [timeout_ms] for the camera's first picture
+  // or for the system to say that it cannot give any. Only cameras reached
+  // through the Camera portal (PipeWire, Linux) wait: their StartCapture returns
+  // at once, and a camera another application holds fails only as PipeWire
+  // links it. Every other camera answers kStartRunning at once.
+  virtual StartOutcome WaitForStart(int timeout_ms, string& why) {
+    why = std::string();
+    return kStartRunning;
+  }
 };
 
